# Katu jobs

From `~/Sites/efemer`.

## Interactive (Ctrl+C must work)

**Never use `-T` for long-running jobs in a terminal.** `-T` disconnects without signaling PHP, so the job keeps running in the container.

```bash
./bin/job jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.RefreshEfemerCz -f
# same as:
docker compose exec php php bin/cli.php jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.Ingest.RefreshEfemerCz -f
```

Kill orphans (after a bad Ctrl+C with `-T`):

```bash
./bin/job jobs:kill
# or force:
./bin/job jobs:kill -f
```

## Scripts / CI / agent (no TTY)

```bash
docker compose exec -T php php bin/cli.php jobs:run App.Classes.Jobs.… -f
docker compose exec -T php php bin/cli.php jobs:loop App.Classes.Jobs.… --interval=21600 -f
docker compose exec -T php php bin/cli.php jobs:kill -f
```

Portable class names use dots instead of backslashes. Pass JSON with `--args='{"key":"value"}'`.

Do not add new `bin/*.php` one-off scripts for ops — add a job under `app/Classes/Jobs/` instead. Legacy `bin/*` stubs only print the job command.

Color logs via `App\Classes\Jobs\ConsoleStyle`. Signals via `App\Classes\Jobs\Signals`.
